IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sa-nouns`

-- Part 2 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia), sections 6 to 13: rules about the meaning of words.
-- Each rule is a function over a small typed description of what the rule operates on.
-- "Unless the contrary intention appears" and the like are asked as a fact: a contrary intention appears, or it does not.
-- Where the text lists with "includes" or "will be construed as including", a case it does not list is NOTHING.

§ `Part 2 -- Definitions and rules about the meaning of words (sections 6 to 13)`

§§ `6 -- Definitions to be read in context`

-- src:272 | Definitions in an Act or a legislative instrument apply to the construction of the Act or instrument except in so far as a contrary intention appears.
@ref s 6 (src:272)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a definition in an Act or legislative instrument applies to its construction` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `7 -- Parts of speech and grammatical forms`

DECLARE `Form of a defined word or phrase` IS ONE OF
    `the word or phrase as defined`
    `another part of speech or grammatical form of it`

-- src:274 | If a word or phrase is defined, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the word or phrase have, unless the contrary intention appears, corresponding meanings.
@ref s 7 (src:274)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of a defined word or phrase`, `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`another form of a defined word or phrase has a corresponding meaning` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
        WHEN `the word or phrase as defined` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `another part of speech or grammatical form of it` THEN IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `8 -- Inclusion of digital material`

-- src:276 | (1) If any type of information or material is capable of being produced in digital form, a word that describes the information or material in its physical form includes a reference to the information or material in its digital form.
@ref s 8(1) (src:276)
GIVEN `the information or material is capable of being produced in digital form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word describing the physical form includes the digital form` MEANS
    JUST `the information or material is capable of being produced in digital form`

DECLARE `Kind of word in section 8(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a verb describing the capture or recording of images or sounds by a recording device`
    `a noun describing the item on which captured or recorded images or sounds are stored or reproduced`
    `a noun describing an item on which there is writing`
    `the word record`
    `any other word`

-- src:277 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a reference to—
-- src:278 | (a) audiotape, photograph, videotape or other word in the form of a verb describing the capture or recording of images or sounds by an audio recording, cinematographic, photographic or videorecording device includes a reference to the capture or recording of images or sounds by a digital device;
-- src:279 | (b) an audiotape, photograph, videotape or other word in the form of a noun describing the item on which images or sounds captured or recorded by an audio recording, cinematographic, photographic or videorecording device are stored or reproduced includes a reference to a digital data storage device;
-- src:280 | (c) a book, paper, plan or other word in the form of a noun describing an item on which there is writing includes a reference to a digital data storage device;
-- src:281 | (d) a record includes information stored in a digital form by means of a digital data storage device.
@ref s 8(2) (src:277-281)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of word in section 8(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference includes its digital counterpart under section 8(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a verb describing the capture or recording of images or sounds by a recording device` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a noun describing the item on which captured or recorded images or sounds are stored or reproduced` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a noun describing an item on which there is writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the word record` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `any other word` THEN NOTHING

-- Section 8(3): a person who keeps information in digital form, and is required to produce it or make it available for inspection,
-- must (unless the body or person otherwise authorises) produce or make available a document that reproduces the information in a form
-- capable of being understood, and doing so complies with the requirement.
-- src:282 | (3) If a person who keeps information in a digital form is required under an Act or a legislative instrument—
-- src:283 | (a) to produce the information or a document containing the information to a body or person; or
-- src:284 | (b) to make the information or a document containing the information available for inspection by a body or person,
-- src:285 | then, unless the body or person otherwise authorises—
-- src:286 | (c) the requirement obliges the person to produce or make available for inspection, as the case may be, a document that reproduces the information in a form capable of being understood by the body or person; and
@ref s 8(3)(c) (src:282-286)
GIVEN `the person keeps the information in digital form and is required to produce it or make it available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body or person otherwise authorises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the requirement obliges producing a document the body or person can understand` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person keeps the information in digital form and is required to produce it or make it available for inspection`) THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `the body or person otherwise authorises` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:282 | (3) If a person who keeps information in a digital form is required under an Act or a legislative instrument—
-- src:283 | (a) to produce the information or a document containing the information to a body or person; or
-- src:284 | (b) to make the information or a document containing the information available for inspection by a body or person,
-- src:285 | then, unless the body or person otherwise authorises—
-- src:287 | (d) the production to the body or person of the document in that form complies with the requirement.
@ref s 8(3)(d) (src:282-287)
GIVEN `the person keeps the information in digital form and is required to produce it or make it available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body or person otherwise authorises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`producing that document complies with the requirement` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person keeps the information in digital form and is required to produce it or make it available for inspection`) THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `the body or person otherwise authorises` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)

§§ `9 -- Words relating to gender`

DECLARE `Who a word implying a gender is applied to` IS ONE OF
    `an individual of the gender the word implies`
    `an individual of another gender`
    `an individual who does not identify as having any particular gender`
    `a body corporate, for section 9`
    `something else, for section 9`

-- src:289 | (1) Every word implying a particular gender will be construed as including every other gender and will also be applicable to an individual who does not identify as having any particular gender.
@ref s 9(1) (src:289)
GIVEN subject IS A `Who a word implying a gender is applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word implying a particular gender is construed as applicable to` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
        WHEN `an individual of the gender the word implies` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an individual of another gender` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an individual who does not identify as having any particular gender` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a body corporate, for section 9` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `something else, for section 9` THEN NOTHING

-- src:290 | (2) Every word implying a particular gender will be construed as including a body corporate as well as an individual.
@ref s 9(2) (src:290)
GIVEN subject IS A `Who a word implying a gender is applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word implying a particular gender includes a body corporate as well as an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
        WHEN `an individual of the gender the word implies` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an individual of another gender` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `an individual who does not identify as having any particular gender` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `a body corporate, for section 9` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `something else, for section 9` THEN NOTHING

-- src:291 | (3) Every phrase consisting of a masculine pronoun and a feminine pronoun joined by the conjunction "or" will be construed as applicable to a body corporate as well as an individual.
@ref s 9(3) (src:291)
GIVEN subject IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a phrase of a masculine and a feminine pronoun joined by "or" is applicable to` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
        WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a partnership` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `an unincorporated body` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `another kind of entity` THEN NOTHING

§§ `10 -- Use of singular and plural`

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF
    `a word in the singular`
    `a word in the plural`

DECLARE `Number asked about` IS ONE OF
    `one`
    `more than one`

-- src:293 | (1) Every word in the singular will be construed as including the plural.
@ref s 10(1) (src:293)
GIVEN word IS A `Number of a word`, asked IS A `Number asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word in the singular is construed as including the plural` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF word EQUALS `a word in the singular` AND asked EQUALS `more than one` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:294 | (2) Every word in the plural will be construed as including the singular.
@ref s 10(2) (src:294)
GIVEN word IS A `Number of a word`, asked IS A `Number asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word in the plural is construed as including the singular` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF word EQUALS `a word in the plural` AND asked EQUALS `one` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:295 | (3) Every word in the plural or singular will be construed as including a body corporate as well as an individual.
@ref s 10(3) (src:295)
GIVEN subject IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word in the plural or singular is construed as including a body corporate as well as an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
        WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a partnership` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `an unincorporated body` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `another kind of entity` THEN NOTHING

§§ `11 -- Meaning of may, must and shall`

DECLARE `Word used in conferring a function` IS ONE OF
    `the word may or a similar expression`
    `the words may not`
    `the word must or shall or a similar expression`

DECLARE `What the entity has` IS ONE OF
    `a discretion as to whether or not to perform the function`
    `a prohibition from performing the function`
    `a requirement to perform the function`

-- Section 11 applies only to an Act or legislative instrument passed after 1 January 1873.
-- src:300 | (4) This section only applies to an Act or a legislative instrument passed after 1 January 1873.
@ref s 11(4) (src:300)
GIVEN `the day the Act or legislative instrument was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 11 applies to an Act or legislative instrument passed on` MEANS
    JUST (`the day the Act or legislative instrument was passed` GREATER THAN (Date 1 1 1873))

-- src:297 | (1) If, in an Act or a legislative instrument, the word "may" or a similar expression is used in conferring a function, the entity on which the function is conferred has a discretion as to whether or not to perform it.
-- src:298 | (2) However, if an Act or a legislative instrument specifies that an entity "may not" perform a function, the entity is prohibited from performing it.
-- src:299 | (3) If, in an Act or a legislative instrument, the word "must" or "shall" (or a similar expression) is used in conferring a function, the entity on which the function is conferred is required to perform it.
@ref s 11(1), (2) and (3) (src:297-299)
GIVEN word IS A `Word used in conferring a function`
      `the day the Act or legislative instrument was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the entity has`
`what the entity on which a function is conferred has` MEANS
    IF `section 11 applies to an Act or legislative instrument passed on` `the day the Act or legislative instrument was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (CONSIDER word
            WHEN `the word may or a similar expression` THEN JUST `a discretion as to whether or not to perform the function`
            WHEN `the words may not` THEN JUST `a prohibition from performing the function`
            WHEN `the word must or shall or a similar expression` THEN JUST `a requirement to perform the function`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `12 -- Meaning of expressions used in legislative instruments`

-- An expression used in a legislative instrument or other instrument made under an Act has the meaning it has in the Act
-- as in force from time to time.
-- src:302 | Expressions used in a legislative instrument or other instrument made under an Act have the same meaning as they have in the Act (as in force from time to time).
@ref s 12 (src:302)
GIVEN `the instrument is made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meaning the expression has in the Act as in force from time to time` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the meaning of an expression used in an instrument made under an Act` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is made under the Act` THEN JUST `the meaning the expression has in the Act as in force from time to time` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `13 -- References to signing or execution of documents`

DECLARE `How a body corporate signs or executes a document` IS ONE OF
    `affixing the common seal of the body to the document`
    `signing the document on behalf of the body in accordance with the Act under which the body is incorporated`
    `signing or executing the document in any other manner permitted by law`
    `a manner of signing or execution that is neither of those and is not permitted by law`

-- src:304 | If an Act or a legislative instrument requires or authorises a document to be signed or executed by a person and the person is a body corporate, the Act or legislative instrument will be taken to authorise—
-- src:305 | (a) the affixing of the common seal of the body to the document, or the signing of the document on behalf of the body, in accordance with the Act (whether or not of this State) under which the body is incorporated; or
-- src:306 | (b) the signing or execution of the document in any other manner permitted by law.
@ref s 13 (src:304-306)
GIVEN `the Act or legislative instrument requires or authorises a document to be signed or executed by a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `How a body corporate signs or executes a document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the Act or legislative instrument requires or authorises a document to be signed or executed by a person` AND `the person is a body corporate`)) THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (CONSIDER manner
            WHEN `affixing the common seal of the body to the document` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `signing the document on behalf of the body in accordance with the Act under which the body is incorporated` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `signing or executing the document in any other manner permitted by law` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `a manner of signing or execution that is neither of those and is not permitted by law` THEN NOTHING)

§§ `Tests`

-- s 6
#ASSERT `a definition in an Act or legislative instrument applies to its construction` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a definition in an Act or legislative instrument applies to its construction` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7
#ASSERT `another form of a defined word or phrase has a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech or grammatical form of it` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `another form of a defined word or phrase has a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech or grammatical form of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `another form of a defined word or phrase has a corresponding meaning` `the word or phrase as defined` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(1)
#ASSERT `a word describing the physical form includes the digital form` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word describing the physical form includes the digital form` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 8(2)
#ASSERT `a reference includes its digital counterpart under section 8(2)` `a verb describing the capture or recording of images or sounds by a recording device` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference includes its digital counterpart under section 8(2)` `a noun describing the item on which captured or recorded images or sounds are stored or reproduced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference includes its digital counterpart under section 8(2)` `a noun describing an item on which there is writing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference includes its digital counterpart under section 8(2)` `the word record` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference includes its digital counterpart under section 8(2)` `any other word` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(3)
#ASSERT `the requirement obliges producing a document the body or person can understand` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement obliges producing a document the body or person can understand` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirement obliges producing a document the body or person can understand` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `producing that document complies with the requirement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `producing that document complies with the requirement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `producing that document complies with the requirement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9
#ASSERT `a word implying a particular gender is construed as applicable to` `an individual of the gender the word implies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word implying a particular gender is construed as applicable to` `an individual of another gender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word implying a particular gender is construed as applicable to` `an individual who does not identify as having any particular gender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word implying a particular gender is construed as applicable to` `something else, for section 9` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a word implying a particular gender includes a body corporate as well as an individual` `a body corporate, for section 9` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word implying a particular gender includes a body corporate as well as an individual` `something else, for section 9` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a phrase of a masculine and a feminine pronoun joined by "or" is applicable to` `a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a phrase of a masculine and a feminine pronoun joined by "or" is applicable to` `an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a phrase of a masculine and a feminine pronoun joined by "or" is applicable to` `a partnership` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10
#ASSERT `a word in the singular is construed as including the plural` `a word in the singular` `more than one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word in the singular is construed as including the plural` `a word in the plural` `more than one` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a word in the singular is construed as including the plural` `a word in the singular` `one` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a word in the plural is construed as including the singular` `a word in the plural` `one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word in the plural is construed as including the singular` `a word in the singular` `one` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a word in the plural is construed as including the singular` `a word in the plural` `more than one` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a word in the plural or singular is construed as including a body corporate as well as an individual` `a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word in the plural or singular is construed as including a body corporate as well as an individual` `an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a word in the plural or singular is construed as including a body corporate as well as an individual` `another kind of entity` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11: 1 January 1873 itself is not "after" it; the next day is.
#ASSERT `section 11 applies to an Act or legislative instrument passed on` (Date 2 1 1873) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 11 applies to an Act or legislative instrument passed on` (Date 1 1 1873) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 11 applies to an Act or legislative instrument passed on` (Date 31 12 1872) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `what the entity on which a function is conferred has` `the word may or a similar expression` (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST `a discretion as to whether or not to perform the function`
#ASSERT `what the entity on which a function is conferred has` `the words may not` (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST `a prohibition from performing the function`
#ASSERT `what the entity on which a function is conferred has` `the word must or shall or a similar expression` (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST `a requirement to perform the function`
#ASSERT `what the entity on which a function is conferred has` `the word must or shall or a similar expression` (Date 1 1 1873) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `what the entity on which a function is conferred has` `the word may or a similar expression` (Date 1 1 1800) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12
#ASSERT `the meaning of an expression used in an instrument made under an Act` TRUE "as the Act now has it" EQUALS JUST "as the Act now has it"
#ASSERT `the meaning of an expression used in an instrument made under an Act` FALSE "as the Act now has it" EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` TRUE TRUE `affixing the common seal of the body to the document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` TRUE TRUE `signing the document on behalf of the body in accordance with the Act under which the body is incorporated` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` TRUE TRUE `signing or executing the document in any other manner permitted by law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` TRUE TRUE `a manner of signing or execution that is neither of those and is not permitted by law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` TRUE FALSE `affixing the common seal of the body to the document` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument is taken to authorise a body corporate to sign or execute in this manner` FALSE TRUE `affixing the common seal of the body to the document` EQUALS JUST FALSE
